= Biography
Research interests, career, and contact details

I am Assoc. Prof. Vo Thi Luu Phuong (published as *Phuong Luu Vo*), an Associate Professor at
the School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University -- Vietnam National
University Ho Chi Minh City, where I lead the *Network Optimization and Distributed Learning*
group.

I received my Ph.D. in Computer Engineering from Kyung Hee University, Korea, and have since
worked on the algorithms behind networked systems: how resources are shared, where content is
placed and how it is delivered, and -- more recently -- how learning can make those decisions
without a full model of the system.

My work combines optimization, network economics, and machine learning. The common thread is
that a network is a shared resource, so almost every interesting question is an optimization
question, and increasingly one that has to be answered from data rather than from a closed-form
solution. Outside research I enjoy teaching and playing classical guitar.

